              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Hint: What happens to a leaky bucket eventually?",
                  "marks": [],
                  "colour": "#268cff"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The bucket is empty at $t=2$. For $t>2$, the model predicts increasing volume, which does not describe a leaking bucket.",
          "worked": "$$V(2)=2^2-4(2)+4=0.$$\nThe bucket is empty after 2 minutes. Since $V(t)=(t-2)^2$, the predicted volume increases after $t=2$, although no water is being added. Time before $t=0$ is outside the stated situation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
